  "foaf:name": "Joint Action on Offshore Freshened Groundwater",
  "sdo:name": "Joint Action on Offshore Freshened Groundwater",
  "sdo:description": "Offshore Freshened Groundwater (OFG) is a potentially strategic resource for coastal water security. Advancing understanding of OFG systems requires research into emplacement history, age, recharge/discharge mechanisms, permeability, porosity, and fluid flow pathways. Studying hydraulic properties, and connectivity between onshore and offshore aquifers is key to assess long-term viability and estimate the sustainable yield. Understanding recharge processes under current conditions should be a prerequisite before any large-scale exploitation, as abstraction could significantly impact the freshwater-saltwater interface. The primary objective of this Joint Call is to act as a “proof of concept” through the launch of a pioneering scientific drilling campaign integrating hydrogeological and geochemical characterisation with pumping tests to validate OFG systems and generate critical data on their distribution, properties, recharge mechanisms, and long-term viability as a resource.",
